By playtesting, we found that our game works better in a digital environment. However, paper playtesting helps to excercise our mental abilities and imagination when it comes to understanding the mechanics of our game, mostly the ghost mechanic. For example, it was a lot easier to understand just how the level was impacted by the ghosts themselves, such as how a ghost landing on a button would make a platform move, or a door open. We started thinking of ideas for new levels, thinking about the chain of events that would have to happen for the player to reach the end of the level.
